ef=3D"https://www.google.com/url?q=3Dhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v%3DuXEY=
uDwm7e4&amp;sa=3DD&amp;source=3Deditors&amp;ust=3D1710480778648688&amp;usg=
=3DAOvVaw3rDAr-iU-jdPsEISSz7brS">lecture video</a></span><span>&nbsp;explai=
ns the same. You can also refer to </span><span class=3D"c5"><a class=3D"c4=
" href=3D"https://www.google.com/url?q=3Dhttps://mecha-mind.medium.com/unde=
rstanding-and-implementing-raft-consensus-protocol-in-python-dd4e9f23b784&a=
mp;sa=3DD&amp;source=3Deditors&amp;ust=3D1710480778648826&amp;usg=3DAOvVaw3=
2bSGWGPyNOVkb26Xo0DvD">this medium blog</a></span><span class=3D"c1">&nbsp;=
implementing Raft in Python.</span></p><p class=3D"c17 c22"><span class=3D"=
c1"></span></p><h2 class=3D"c30" id=3D"h.gc2slk4z0iau"><span class=3D"c6">2=
. </span><span class=3D"c6">Storage and Database </span><span class=3D"c6">=
Operations</span></h2><p class=3D"c12"><span>As mentioned in the introducti=
on, we are</span><span>&nbsp;building a database that stores key-value pair=
s </span><span>mapping string (key) to string (value)</span><span class=3D"=
c1">. The Raft Nodes serve the client for storing and retrieving these key-=
value pairs and replicating this data among other nodes in a fault-tolerant=
 manner.</span></p><p class=3D"c9"><span class=3D"c1"></span></p><ol class=
=3D"c0 lst-kix_zhiyg7gae7ze-0 start" start=3D"1"><li class=3D"c8 c27 li-bul=
let-0"><span>The nodes must be persistent, i.e., even after stopping the no=
de, the data (logs) must be stored somewhere (in any </span><span class=3D"=
c5"><a class=3D"c4" href=3D"https://www.google.com/url?q=3Dhttps://en.wikip=
edia.org/wiki/Human-readable_medium_and_data%23:~:text%3DIn%2520computing%2=
52C%2520a%2520human%252Dreadable,rather%2520than%2520as%2520binary%2520data=
.&amp;sa=3DD&amp;source=3Deditors&amp;ust=3D1710480778649368&amp;usg=3DAOvV=
aw2iTtLI_tcIXlKrYAfRSSy1">human-readable format</a></span><span>, e.g., .tx=
t) along with other important metadata (commitLength, Term, and NodeID whic=
h the current node voted for in this term) and retrieved when the node star=
ts again</span><span class=3D"c1">.</span></li></ol><p class=3D"c9"><span c=
lass=3D"c1"></span></p><ol class=3D"c0 lst-kix_zhiyg7gae7ze-0" start=3D"2">=
<li class=3D"c8 c27 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c1">Follow the following na=
