Vote Reply RPC and its own) to run out before acquiring its own lease.</spa=
n></li><li class=3D"c13 c18 li-bullet-0"><span>Once in the Leader state </s=
pan><span class=3D"c20">and the old lease timer has run out, the node start=
s its lease timer,</span><span>&nbsp;appends a </span><span class=3D"c6">NO=
-OP</span><span>&nbsp;entry to the log, and sends heartbeats to all other n=
odes.</span></li><li class=3D"c13 c18 li-bullet-0"><span>Implementing Leade=
r Lease requires additional changes, specified in detail in a later section=
 on </span><span class=3D"c6">Modifications to Standard Raft</span><span>.<=
/span></li></ol><h2 class=3D"c30" id=3D"h.ur5ve0ec9o6t"><span class=3D"c29 =
c6">6. Log Replication Functionalities</span></h2><p class=3D"c21"><span cl=
ass=3D"c1">The nodes perform the following functionality in order to replic=
ate the logs correctly to all nodes and maintain log integrity.</span></p><=
p class=3D"c21 c22"><span class=3D"c1"></span></p><ol class=3D"c0 lst-kix_i=
9ca40vqrhsb-0 start" start=3D"1"><li class=3D"c10 li-bullet-0"><span class=
=3D"c2">Periodic Heartbeats:</span></li></ol><ol class=3D"c0 lst-kix_i9ca40=
vqrhsb-1 start" start=3D"1"><li class=3D"c21 c18 li-bullet-0"><span>The lea=
der sends periodic heartbeats </span><span class=3D"c6">(~1 second/heartbea=
t)</span><span class=3D"c1">&nbsp;to all nodes to maintain its leader state=
.</span></li><li class=3D"c21 c18 li-bullet-0"><span>This heartbeat utilize=
s the same appendEntriesRPC.</span></li><li class=3D"c12 c18 li-bullet-0"><=
span class=3D"c20">The leader also reacquires its lease at each heartbeat b=
y restarting the lease timer and propagating the lease duration </span><spa=
n class=3D"c20 c6">(</span><span class=3D"c6 c25">~10 seconds</span><span c=
lass=3D"c6 c20">)</span><span class=3D"c1 c20">. </span></li><li class=3D"c=
12 c18 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c1 c20">The leader needs to step down if=
 it cannot reacquire the lease (did not receive a successful acknowledgment=
 from the majority of followers within the lease duration).</span></li><li =
class=3D"c12 c18 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c20">At each heartbeat, the fo=
llowers also monitor and keep track of the duration of the lease.</span><sp=
an class=3D"c1"><br></span></li></ol><ol class=3D"c0 lst-kix_i9ca40vqrhsb-0=
" start=3D"2"><li class=3D"c10 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c2">Replicate Lo=
g Request:</span></li></ol><ol class=3D"c0 lst-kix_i9ca40vqrhsb-1 start" st=
art=3D"1"><li class=3D"c21 c18 li-bullet-0"><span>Whenever the leader recei=
ves a client SET request, the appendEntriesRPC is used to replicate the log=
 to all nodes. </span><span class=3D"c1 c20">(In the case of the GET reques=
t, the value can immediately be returned as long as the lease is acquired).=
</span></li><li class=3D"c21 c18 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c1">To synchro=
nize a follower's log with the leader's, the leader identifies the latest m=
atching log entry (same PrevLogIndex and PrevLogTerm), removes entries in t=
he follower's log beyond that point, and transmits all subsequent leader en=
tries. </span></li><li class=3D"c21 c18 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c1">Onc=
e the majority of nodes have replicated the log, a SUCCESS reply is sent to=
 the client. Otherwise, it replies with a FAIL message. (Refer to the Clien=
t Interaction section)</span></li><li class=3D"c21 c18 li-bullet-0"><span c=
lass=3D"c1">Successful AppendEntries ensure log consistency for the remaind=
er of the term.<br></span></li></ol><ol class=3D"c0 lst-kix_i9ca40vqrhsb-0"=
 start=3D"3"><li class=3D"c10 li-bullet-0"><span class=3D"c2">Replicate Log=
 Reply:</span></li></ol><ol class=3D"c0 lst-kix_i9ca40vqrhsb-1 start" start=
=3D"1"><li class=3D"c21 c18 li-bullet-0"><span>A node accepts an AppendEntr=
iesRPC request only when certain conditions are met. Please refer to the ps=
eudo-code for more information.</span></li></ol><h2 class=3D"c30" id=3D"h.t=
0bervjqv4iq"><span class=3D"c6">7</span><span class=3D"c6">. Committing Ent=
ries</span></h2><p class=3D"c21"><span class=3D"c1">Conditions that need to=
 be satisfied for the nodes to commit an entry have been specified in the p=
